# Canonical decision-manifest vocabulary for phased-execution.
# SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH (F5 pattern, like gates.env) — but the OWNER here is
# viewer/shared/decisions-model.js, and this file is its bash twin: sourced by
# scripts/phase-graph.sh (--decisions, lint F25), scripts/decisions.sh (the
# twin writer) and scripts/phase-outcome.sh (--needs). viewer/test/
# decisions-model.test.ts asks bash for every list below and holds it to the
# JS owner word for word, so the two can never disagree. Change BOTH.
#
# Plain KEY="VALUE" (sourced by bash 3.2) — space-separated tokens.
#
#   DECISION_KEYS    — the seventeen decisions a run can need (chapter 13 §1.1);
#                      one `## Decisions` row per key, and the word a ruling, an
#                      errand and a `needs-human` reason carry as decisionKey.
#   DECISION_STATES  — answered | outstanding | waived.
#   DECISION_SOURCES — plan | run | default | ruling.
#   NEED_CLASSES     — the blocker classes `--needs` also accepts, as the SHORT
#                      form of a key (credential→credentials,
#                      permission→permission.policy, gate→gates,
#                      external→waits; lock names no row).
DECISION_KEYS="permission.policy permission.destructive credentials accounts mcp gates verification.person-check qa.exhausted waits human-acts ambiguity budgets resume.on-restart plan-health stop relay announce"
DECISION_STATES="answered outstanding waived"
DECISION_SOURCES="plan run default ruling"
NEED_CLASSES="lock permission credential gate external"
